          "type": "registry:page",
          "target": "app/(protected)/inbox/actions.ts"
        },
        {
          "path": "registry/items/sendo-inbox/app/(protected)/inbox/inbox-config.ts",
          "type": "registry:page",
          "target": "app/(protected)/inbox/inbox-config.ts"
        },
        {
          "path": "registry/items/sendo-inbox/hooks/use-sendo-realtime.ts",
          "type": "registry:hook",
          "target": "hooks/use-sendo-realtime.ts"
        },
        {
          "path": "registry/items/sendo-inbox/lib/sendo-realtime.ts",
          "type": "registry:lib",
          "target": "lib/sendo-realtime.ts"
        }
      ],
      "docs": "Sendo inbox installed at /inbox (app/(protected)/inbox). It needs @sendo/sendo-webhook (lib/sendo.ts) and @sendo/sendo-schema. Before using it: (1) implement requireUser() in app/(protected)/inbox/inbox-config.ts with your app's auth (it throws until then, so the inbox fails closed) and return the operator's tenant; (2) replace sendo_can_access_tenant(tenant_id) in your database so operators only see their tenant; (3) mount <Toaster /> from components/ui/sonner in your root layout; (4) for live updates set NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_URL and NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY and make lib/sendo-realtime.ts return a client with the operator's session (createBrowserClient from @supabase/ssr if you use it). Override texts with <Inbox strings={{ ... }} />; motion tokens live in components/sendo/motion.css (under prefers-reduced-motion opacity and colour still fade and transform movement is removed)."
    }
  ]
